<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reinhard Heydrich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1904">1904</a>–<a href="/years/1942">1942</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Reinhard Heydrich was a senior SS officer, head of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reich-security-main-office">Reich Security Main Office</a> and one of the main architects of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holocaust">Holocaust</a>, who chaired the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wannsee-conference">Wannsee Conference</a> in January 1942. Appointed deputy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reich-protector">Reich Protector</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a> in 1941, he ruled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechs">Czechs</a> by terror. Czechoslovak parachutists mortally wounded him in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> in May 1942, and the Nazis destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lidice">Lidice</a> in reprisal.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/reinhard-heydrich.jpg" alt="Reinhard Heydrich" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Uncredited photographer. US National Archives and Records Administration (NARA ): Unrestricted access and use. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reinhard_Heydrich_1940_Portrait_(3x4_cropped)_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
